  "IMPORTANT_alpha4_artifact": "The by_alpha table's alpha=4 SFS (0.396, the highest of any alpha) is NOT evidence of better faithfulness at that perturbation strength -- it is a coincidental artifact of the model's near-constant-response pathology (same phenomenon as project_sgf_e2_finding.md / E4's confound). The model's reported velocities are drawn from a tiny fixed palette (0.3, 0.5, 0.6, 0.84, 1.5, 1.875, 3.5 m/s) that barely varies with the actual displayed calibration. At alpha=4 specifically, EVERY item (all clips/orientations/seeds) happens to land on the same (base=0.5, scaled=1.5) pair -- a content-independent 3x ratio that coincidentally sits close to the ideal alpha=4 log-ratio target, scoring artificially high. At other alphas the same small palette produces ratios far from ideal, scoring low. This is luck-of-the-draw from a small discrete output set landing near a target by chance, not a real alpha-dependent faithfulness effect -- do not report the by_alpha spread (0.331) as showing the model is 'more faithful under strong perturbation.' The orientation and seed axes did NOT show this coincidental-alignment problem (their spreads, 0.046 and 0.087, are genuine measures of low variability, not itself a positive faithfulness signal either, just consistently low).",
